lisa-design:
- Hand-laid SVG, no graph library: a column per event (time order, events only a decision names get a placeholder), the actions of its fired decisions stacked below, arrows labelled <RuleSet>/<rule>. Dispatch is a solid rectangle, set/effect/notify/cancel/link/requestApproval dotted. State is stroke colour plus the state text.
- Joins (graph.ts): dispatch -> task by provenance {event, ruleSet, rule}, the n-th dispatch of a decision to its n-th task by creation; task -> runs by spec.task; run -> factory.run.completed/.failed by facts.run.id (solid link). A rule's own effect -> Effect with empty spec.task, idempotencyKey evt/<event>/... and the factory.ccf.dev/rule label (the key the applier writes). Approvals by order of requestApproval actions (Decision.actions has no names). Inferred (dashed): the first later non-factory.* event whose actor.isFactory and object.ref is one the action touched (rule effect target, the task's effects' targets, Result data.pr).
- A fired decision whose rail held it shows the rail verdict (Suppressed/Deferred) as the action's state unless an object was created anyway (a deferred dispatch that later ran shows the task phase).
- Clicking an action opens DecisionWhy for its decision (the timeline's panel); clicking an event switches to the Timeline tab and opens that row (focus prop). Tabs reuse UI-1c's TabList; the tab is in ?tab=.
- Timeline rows are per event; tasks/runs/effects are shown under the action that created them, and anything no action accounts for goes to "Other activity" so nothing is lost from the old flat timeline. The newest row starts open.
- The mock pipeline work item (wi_01JAC0PIPELINE…) exercises every link; adding it to the list changed the board specs' counts.
